      "content": "Traditionalist theologians often argue that changes in how society defines marriage and family undermine the natural order as intended by divine creation. They claim that marriage should be exclusively between a man and a woman because this is presented as a fundamental design from God, grounded in ancient texts and normative historical practices. Moreover, they stress the importance of procreation and societal stability that they believe traditional marital frameworks foster. Lastly, many traditionalist theologians hold that redefining marriage by same-sex couples, though morally equivalent in some forms, does not align with their interpretation of God's intention for marriage and the family structure.",
